    "title": "50-year-old woman was unintended victim in fatal targeted shooting - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Chloe Williams Staff Writer ,\n6 days ago A 50-year-old woman was killed when two suspects opened fire on a car at a Hammond gas station early Thursday, June 4, firing 70 to 80 shots into the vehicle. Hammond Police Chief Edwin Bergeron said that afternoon that the shooting was a targeted incident and not random, but the victim, Patricia Sheppard, 50, was not the intended target. Read full article",
